 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Take a few deep breaths, and use your hands to mark the pages of what you like and don't like. A spot for everything in between helps too. Order a little of each, and see for yourself. If you still doubt, ask to taste the pasta instead. Which is easier? Ordering few bites of pasta, or ordering a full pasta dish and hoping for the best? Not always. Some restaurants do a big stock change every few months, so the special might be the old sauce. Ask to see the kitchen, and you'll often see it being made. Busy places with long queues love to keep old pasta. Faster places with few guests actually listen to their pasta going off.",
